		'sticker.early' => array(
			'en' => 'In Pima County, early voters got their own sticker. In 2022 the Recorder\'s Office made it trilingual: "I voted" in English, "A:ñi \'ant wodalt" in Tohono O\'odham and "Yo Voté" in Spanish, a nod to the Tohono O\'odham Nation\'s ancestral homelands. It went to early voters by mail and in person. Election Day voters got the standard oval sticker.',
